WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.160
The CSF Core is the main taxonomy of CSF 2.0 outcomes.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:11.700
At the highest level, it is organized into six Functions: Govern, Identify, Protect,

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.720
Detect, Respond, and Recover.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:19.420
These Functions are a way to talk about the major areas of cybersecurity risk management.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:23.400
They should be addressed concurrently rather than treated as a strict sequence.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:27.140
Governance informs the work, identification supports protection,

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.120
detection supports response, and recovery strengthens resilience.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:33.500
Each Function contains Categories.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:36.680
A Category groups related outcomes within that Function.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:42.820
For example, a Category may deal with asset management, identity management, awareness,

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:46.560
monitoring, incident response, or recovery planning.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:51.180
Categories help teams move from broad Function language to areas of work that can be

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.200
owned,

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.500
assessed, and improved.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.280
Each Category contains Subcategories.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:00.140
A Subcategory describes a more specific outcome.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:04.440
A Subcategory may point toward an outcome such as maintaining an inventory,

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.740
managing identities, protecting data, collecting logs, planning response,

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:10.560
or testing recovery.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:14.300
The Subcategory describes what the organization wants to achieve,

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.680
not one mandatory way to achieve it.

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.580
That distinction matters.

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:22.640
The Core describes outcomes, not a single implementation path.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:27.020
Two organizations may pursue the same outcome with different technologies, procedures,

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:31.000
roles, evidence, suppliers, and risk decisions.

00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:37.220
CSF 2.0 gives them a common structure for describing the outcome and discussing progress.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:42.000
It does not remove the need to decide what implementation fits the system, mission,

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:43.900
and threat context.
